---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 2</p>
  <h1>Present continuous: <em>happening now</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Show what is in progress at this moment: <span class="ex">I’m waiting for the bus</span>, <span class="ex">She’s talking to a client</span>, and <span class="ex">Are they working?</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 55–65 min</span>
    <span class="tag">am / is / are + verb-ing</span>
    <span class="tag">happening now</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>See routine and right now side by side.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Build be + verb-ing.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Make questions, negatives, and short answers.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe this exact moment in your life.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">The present continuous is the grammar of live description: what is in progress at this moment, or temporarily around now.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. You will need <b>am, is, are</b> again in a minute.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="works">works</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="work">work</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="am" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a teacher at a language school. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the verb to be)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>My parents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> doctors. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the verb to be)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Omar <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="works" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> long hours at the clinic. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(present simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A break at the office</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"I work at a bank downtown. Right now I’m having lunch with a coworker. We’re sitting outside, and she’s telling me about her new apartment."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which sentence describes a routine, something generally true?</li>
      <li>Which actions are happening at this moment?</li>
      <li>What small verb comes before each <span class="ex">-ing</span> word?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: choose the pattern</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the subject to choose <b>am</b>, <b>is</b>, or <b>are</b>. Two gaps need the <b>-ing</b> verb itself.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="working">working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="waiting">waiting</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="am" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> waiting for the elevator.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> talking to a client.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> working late tonight.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> raining outside.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Marcos is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from home today.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>We are <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="waiting" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> for the train.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: am, is, are + verb-ing</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Every present continuous sentence has two verbs: a form of <span class="ex">be</span> that agrees with the subject, and a verb ending in <span class="ex">-ing</span> that names the activity.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>I</th><th>you / we / they</th><th>he / she / it</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>positive</b></td><td>I’m working.</td><td>We’re working.</td><td>She’s working.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>negative</b></td><td>I’m not working.</td><td>We aren’t working.</td><td>She isn’t working.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>question</b></td><td>Am I talking too fast?</td><td>Are you working?</td><td>Is she working?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Short answers use only the be verb: <span class="ex">Yes, I am. / Yes, she is. / No, they aren’t.</span> Never repeat the <span class="ex">-ing</span> verb, and do not contract a positive short answer.</p>

  <h2>Get to the root: an action viewed from inside</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The present continuous does more than say “now.” It presents an action as <strong>open and in progress</strong>. Imagine a video with a beginning and an end. The speaker places the camera somewhere between those two points. At that camera moment, the action is not finished.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>The mental picture</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">She is writing a report.</span></p>
    <p>The sentence does not tell us when she started or when she will finish. It tells us that the activity is open around the time we are talking about. She may pause for coffee and still be “writing a report” as her current project.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Has the report-writing started? <strong>Yes.</strong></li>
      <li>Is it presented as finished? <strong>No.</strong></li>
      <li>Must her pen be moving at this exact second? <strong>Not always.</strong> It can be a temporary activity around now.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h3>Why there are two verbs</h3>
  <p>English builds this meaning in two parts. The verb <span class="ex">be</span> carries the subject and tense: <span class="ex">I am</span>, <span class="ex">she is</span>, <span class="ex">they are</span>. The <span class="ex">-ing</span> verb names the unfolding activity. That is why <span class="ex">She working</span> is incomplete: the sentence has an activity, but no finite verb to anchor it.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>part</th><th>job</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>am / is / are</b></td><td>agrees with the subject; makes negatives and questions</td><td><span class="ex">Is</span> she working? She <span class="ex">isn’t</span> working.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>verb-ing</b></td><td>shows the activity as unfolding</td><td>She is <span class="ex">working</span>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Follow the moving part</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">She is working. → Is she working? → She isn’t working.</span></p>
    <p>Only <span class="ex">is</span> moves to the front or becomes negative. The <span class="ex">-ing</span> verb never changes. This is why <span class="ex">Do you are working?</span> mixes two different systems and is not the target form.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Spelling the -ing form</h3>
  <p>We add <span class="ex">-ing</span> to the base verb, but spelling sometimes protects the original sound. Most verbs simply add <span class="ex">-ing</span>; a few need one small change first.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>base verb</th><th>rule</th><th>-ing form</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>work, wait</td><td>just add <b>-ing</b></td><td><span class="ex">work → working</span>, <span class="ex">wait → waiting</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>make, write</td><td>drop the silent <b>e</b></td><td><span class="ex">make → making</span>, <span class="ex">write → writing</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>run, sit</td><td>double the final consonant after one short stressed vowel</td><td><span class="ex">run → running</span>, <span class="ex">sit → sitting</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>study, stay</td><td>keep the <b>y</b></td><td><span class="ex">study → studying</span>, <span class="ex">stay → staying</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>lie, die</td><td>change <b>ie</b> to <b>y</b></td><td><span class="ex">lie → lying</span>, <span class="ex">die → dying</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the natural chunk</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the subject first, then the context: is the sentence positive or negative? Choose the chunk people really say.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="’m working">’m working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="’s working">’s working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are working">are working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="isn’t working">isn’t working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="aren’t working">aren’t working</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="’m working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from home this week, so call me on my cell.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>My sister <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="’s working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> in Chicago this month. She likes her new team.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The builders <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the roof right now, so it’s noisy.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The elevator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="isn’t working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> today, so take the stairs.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="aren’t working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> this Friday. The office is closed for the holiday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Dan <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="’s working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> late tonight, so don’t wait for him for dinner.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>You and Priya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the same report, so please share your notes.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>My headphones <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="aren’t working" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> again, so I can’t hear the call.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Present simple or present continuous?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The difference is usually not the action itself. It is the <strong>speaker’s viewpoint</strong>. The present simple looks at a stable pattern from the outside; the present continuous looks at an open situation from the inside.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>present simple: routine or fact</th><th>present continuous: now, temporary, around now</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">I work at home.</span><br>That is my normal arrangement.</td><td><span class="ex">I’m working at home today.</span><br>This is the temporary situation now.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">She takes the bus.</span><br>That is her routine.</td><td><span class="ex">She’s taking a taxi.</span><br>That is happening on this occasion.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">What do you do?</span><br>What is your job or routine?</td><td><span class="ex">What are you doing?</span><br>What activity is in progress?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Time expressions are clues, not automatic rules. <span class="ex">Every day, usually</span> often support the present simple; <span class="ex">now, today, at the moment</span> often support the continuous. First understand the meaning, then use the clue.</p>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>One useful limit</h3>
    <p>Some verbs normally describe a state, not an unfolding action: <span class="ex">know, understand, want, need, like</span>. At this level, prefer <span class="ex">I understand</span> and <span class="ex">I need help</span>, not <span class="ex">I’m understanding</span> or <span class="ex">I’m needing help</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: type the question word or short answer</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Questions start with <b>Am</b>, <b>Is</b>, or <b>Are</b>. Short answers use the be verb alone, never the <b>-ing</b> verb.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Are" aria-label="answer 1" /> you working right now?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Yes, I <input class="answer-input" data-answer="am" aria-label="answer 2" />.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Is" aria-label="answer 3" /> Lena driving to the airport?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>No, she <input class="answer-input" data-answer="isn’t" aria-label="answer 4" />.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Am" aria-label="answer 5" /> I speaking too fast?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>No, you <input class="answer-input" data-answer="aren’t" aria-label="answer 6" />.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A message from a coworker</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Where are you? We’re waiting outside the restaurant. Dana is parking the car, and Tom is holding a table for us inside. I’m looking at the menu now, and everything looks great. Are you still finishing that report?"</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You followed a real conversation about right now.">
    <h3>Drill 3: read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="outside the restaurant">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Where is the group waiting?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="outside the restaurant">outside the restaurant</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="inside the office">inside the office</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at the station">at the station</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="parking the car">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What is Dana doing right now?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="parking the car">parking the car</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="holding a table">holding a table</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="reading the menu">reading the menu</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the person reading the message">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Who is probably still working?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the person reading the message">the person reading the message</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Tom">Tom</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana">Dana</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="is she taking the train">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the question. Remember: is moves in front of the subject.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="taking">taking</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">Is</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="train">train</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">she</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="we aren’t watching the game tonight">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the negative</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence. Only aren’t carries the negative.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="watching">watching</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="we">We</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="game">game</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="aren’t">aren’t</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="tonight">tonight</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="working" data-fix="She is working at the hospital now." data-why="The -ing verb cannot stand alone. Add is: she is working.">
    <h3>Drill 6: two verbs, not one</h3>
    <p>One small verb is missing. Tap the word that cannot stand alone.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">She</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="working">working</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hospital">at the hospital</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="now">now.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="do" data-fix="Are you working today?" data-why="Present continuous questions move are in front of the subject. Do belongs to the present simple system.">
    <h3>Drill 7: one system at a time</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="do">Do</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are working">are working</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="today">today?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: say it, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the cue, say the full sentence aloud, then reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I’m taking notes. Change to he.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He’s taking notes.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> They’re watching the game. Make it negative.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They aren’t watching the game.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> She’s cooking dinner. Ask the question.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Is she cooking dinner?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Are you listening? Answer yes.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Yes, I am.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> He drives to work. Make it about right now.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He’s driving to work right now.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> We’re waiting for the bus. Change to she.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She’s waiting for the bus.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Live camera:</b> Describe five things happening in your room, on your street, or on your screen right now. <span class="ex">The neighbors are cooking. A bus is passing.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Family radar:</b> Guess what three family members or friends are doing at this moment. <span class="ex">My brother is probably driving home now.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask the teacher:</b> Ask five questions about this exact moment and listen for the short answers. <span class="ex">Are you drinking coffee? Are you sitting near a window? What are you looking at?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Not true now:</b> Say three things that are not happening right now. <span class="ex">I’m not driving. It isn’t raining. My phone isn’t ringing.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Today is different:</b> Contrast one routine with today. <span class="ex">I usually take the bus, but today I’m walking.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “The present continuous needs two verbs: a form of ______ and the verb ending in ______. For a question, ______ moves in front of the subject. The present simple describes a routine; the present continuous describes what is happening ______.”</p>
    <p>Then say one positive sentence, one negative sentence, and one question about this exact moment.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. You can describe what is happening right now, and what usually happens.">
    <h3>Final quiz: forms and meaning</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is raining">
